          "id": "fb2af40b-6341-4bd6-aa3a-9740fbe15716",
          "targetSpanId": "de414cb2-bdb0-45a0-96f1-92c88e0c2175",
          "sourceAttachment": "middle",
          "targetAttachment": "start",
          "annotation": "Railroads change the dynamics of military mobilization—because it's possible to mobilize and attack in days without long transit delays, mobilizing fast becomes imperative. This is one of the reasons why the Great Powers rushed into WWI—each country didn't want to risk being swiftly defeated by their rivals before their own army had mobilized.  "
